Index,SS / Module,Feature,Test Case Name,Test Description,Meta Test Description,Speed,Mode,Memory Start Offset,Memory End Offset,Remarks,Test Steps / Procedure,Meta Test Steps / Procedure,Impacted Registers,Meta Impacted Registers,Validation / Acceptance Criteria,Meta Validation / Acceptance Criteria,Code Generation (Required / Not),Meta Headers,Meta Macros,Meta Arrays
"1","GPIO","Supports AHB 32-bit for the programming of CSR","gpio_reg_wr_rd_test","Verify GPIO register accessibility and integrity by checking masked default reset values and performing masked write/readback tests over a defined set of addresses. For each register in the test list, read the value (with bit0 masked out) and compare against the expected default. Then, for six data patterns, write the pattern masked by the per-register write mask and read back masked by the read mask; compute the expected value by combining writable bits from the pattern and non-writable bits from the default. Declare pass if no mismatches are detected; otherwise fail. Addresses and masks are provided via arrays; unresolved register macro MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8, unresolved register macro MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_9, unresolved register macro MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_10, unresolved register macro MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_11, unresolved register macro MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_12, unresolved register macro MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_13, unresolved register macro MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_14, unresolved register macro MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_15, unresolved register macro MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_16, unresolved register macro MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_17, unresolved register macro MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_18, unresolved register macro MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_19, unresolved register macro MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_20, unresolved register macro MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_21, unresolved register macro MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_22, unresolved register macro MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_23, unresolved register macro MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_24, unresolved register macro MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_25, unresolved register macro MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_26, unresolved register macro MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_27.","test_case() calls chk_rst_val() then chk_rd_wr(), and finishes with finish(1) on any failure else finish(0). In chk_rst_val(): iterates i from 0 to CNT-1; obtains addr from addr_array[i]; if skip_rst_array[i] == 1, skip; if read_mask_array[i] == 0x00000000, skip; otherwise data_rd = read_reg(addr); data = (data_rd & 0xfffffffe); compare data with default_value_array[i]; on mismatch, increment def_fail_cnt and print failure. In chk_rd_wr(): for each pattern in chk_val[6] = {0xffffffff,0xaaaaaaaa,0x55555555,0xf5f5f5f5,0xA5A5A5A5,0xffff0000}, set data_wr to the pattern; for each i in [0,CNT): get addr = addr_array[i]; if skip_array[i] == 1, continue; if write_mask_array[i] == 0x00000000, continue; else write_reg(addr, (data_wr & write_mask_array[i])). Then read back for verification: for each i, skip if skip_array[i] == 1 or if write_mask_array[i] == 0x00000000 or if read_mask_array[i] == 0x00000000; else data_rd = (read_reg(addr) & read_mask_array[i]); wr_n = (write_mask_array[i] ^ 0xffffffff); exp_val = ((data_wr & read_mask_array[i] & write_mask_array[i]) | (wr_n & read_mask_array[i] & default_value_array[i])); if data_rd != exp_val, increment wr_fail_cnt and print failure. Disabled utility soft_reset_chk() shows a potential soft-reset sequence using SOFT_RST_REG_ADDRESS and SOFT_RST_REG_DATA under #ifdef 0.","NA","NA","NA","NA","NA","1. For each register address listed in the test address array, if readable and not marked to skip, read the register, mask out bit0, and compare to the expected default value; log any mismatch. 2. For each of six data patterns, for each register address that is writable and not marked to skip, write the pattern masked by the register’s write mask. 3. For each written register that is both writable and readable, read back the value masked by the read mask, compute the expected value by combining writable bits from the pattern and non-writable bits from the default, and compare; log any mismatch. 4. Declare the test PASS if no default-value or write/read mismatches are detected; otherwise declare FAIL.","1) test_case(): invoke chk_rst_val(); then invoke chk_rd_wr(); if (def_fail_cnt > 0 || wr_fail_cnt > 0) finish(1); else finish(0). 2) chk_rst_val(): for (i=0; i<CNT; i++): addr = addr_array[i]; if (skip_rst_array[i] == 1) continue; if (read_mask_array[i] == 0x00000000) continue; data_rd = read_reg(addr); data = (data_rd & 0xfffffffe); if (data == default_value_array[i]) PASS else { def_fail_cnt++; print failure }. 3) chk_rd_wr(): define unsigned int chk_val[6]={0xffffffff,0xaaaaaaaa,0x55555555,0xf5f5f5f5,0xA5A5A5A5,0xffff0000}; for each pattern data_wr in chk_val: (a) Write phase: for (i=0; i<CNT; i++): addr = addr_array[i]; if (skip_array[i] == 1) continue; if (write_mask_array[i] == 0x00000000) continue; write_reg(addr, (data_wr & write_mask_array[i])). (b) Read/verify phase: for (i=0; i<CNT; i++): addr = addr_array[i]; if (skip_array[i] == 1) continue; if (write_mask_array[i] == 0x00000000) continue; if (read_mask_array[i] == 0x00000000) continue; data_rd = (read_reg(addr) & read_mask_array[i]); wr_n = (write_mask_array[i] ^ 0xffffffff); exp_val = ((data_wr & read_mask_array[i] & write_mask_array[i]) | (wr_n & read_mask_array[i] & default_value_array[i])); if (data_rd == exp_val) PASS else { wr_fail_cnt++; print failure }. 4) soft_reset_chk() [disabled]: read_reg(SOFT_RST_REG_ADDRESS); write_reg(SOFT_RST_REG_ADDRESS, SOFT_RST_REG_DATA); wait_on(1000); write_reg(SOFT_RST_REG_ADDRESS, default_value); wait_on(1000).","UNRESOLVED(MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8); UNRESOLVED(MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_9); UNRESOLVED(MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_10); UNRESOLVED(MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_11); UNRESOLVED(MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_12); UNRESOLVED(MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_13); UNRESOLVED(MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_14); UNRESOLVED(MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_15); UNRESOLVED(MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_16); UNRESOLVED(MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_17); UNRESOLVED(MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_18); UNRESOLVED(MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_19); UNRESOLVED(MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_20); UNRESOLVED(MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_21); UNRESOLVED(MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_22); UNRESOLVED(MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_23); UNRESOLVED(MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_24); UNRESOLVED(MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_25); UNRESOLVED(MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_26); UNRESOLVED(MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_27); UNRESOLVED(GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8_DEFAULT_VAL); UNRESOLVED(GPIO_GP0_GPIO_9